course: dictionary
lesson: 3989
title: One word, many places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word gallery is a good example. «Felix Gonzalez-Torres made a pile of sweets, and the gallery refills it.» Here a gallery is a place where art is shown, because artists make things like this for people to see.
explain: «The photo gallery on my tablet» is a different meaning. The word photo tells you it is about pictures, so a gallery here is the place where your photos are kept.
explain: «A whisper can travel round a curved wall in a whispering gallery.» Curved wall and whisper are your clues. This gallery is a curved room or passage, not a room of paintings. Always ask: which meaning fits the clues in this sentence?
fact: A gallery can be a building or room where paintings, sculptures and other art are shown.
fact: A gallery can also be a raised floor or balcony inside a big building, like a theatre or church, where people sit or look down.
fact: A gallery can be a long, narrow room or passage.
fact: On a phone or computer, your gallery is the place where your photos are kept.
fact: «Play to the gallery» means to show off to please the crowd.
exercise: «In the dark deep-sea gallery, fish glow with their own light.» What does gallery most likely mean here? | *A room in a museum where things are shown | A boat that carries fish | A dark sea cave | A kind of deep-sea fish
exercise: «A whisper can travel round a curved wall in a whispering gallery.» What is a whispering gallery? | A loud music hall | A place where people go to tell secrets | A type of painting | *A curved room or passage where a quiet voice can be heard from far away
exercise: «A museum keeps important objects safe; a gallery mostly shows art.» What does a gallery mostly show? | Dinosaurs | *Art | Mummies | Machines
test: «Tom pulled silly faces to play to the gallery.» What does play to the gallery mean? | Play a game with lots of people | *Show off to please the crowd | Sit in the top seats of a theatre | Draw a picture of the crowd
test: «Mia saved her holiday photos in the gallery on her phone.» What does gallery mean here? | A raised balcony in a theatre | *The place where your photos are kept | A room full of paintings | A long, narrow passage
exam: «Every artist learns by painting a copy of a masterpiece in a gallery.» Which meaning of gallery fits this sentence best? | A balcony where people look down | The place where your photos are kept | *A building or room where art is shown | A long, narrow passage
